          "zh": "弗吉尼亚数据中心遭受千兆瓦级电力中断"
        },
        "tl_dr": {
          "en": "Power outages due to transmission line faults and equipment failures have disrupted data centers in Ashburn, Virginia, impacting multiple gigawatts of grid load.",
          "zh": "弗吉尼亚州阿什本的数据中心因输电线路故障和设备失效而遭遇电力中断，影响了数千兆瓦的电网负荷。"
        },
        "key_takeaways": {
          "en": [
            "On July 22, 2026, a transmission line fault in Ashburn, Virginia, disconnected over 3 gigawatts of load from the grid.",
            "Two years prior, approximately 60 Virginia facilities experienced a 1,500-megawatt outage due to a single failed surge arrester.",
            "Ashburn, Virginia, is identified as the heart of the world's largest data center cluster."
          ],
          "zh": [
            "2026年7月22日，弗吉尼亚州阿什本的一条输电线路故障导致电网超过3千兆瓦的负荷在数秒内脱落。",
            "两年前，一个浪涌抑制器故障导致弗吉尼亚州大约60个设施中断了1,500兆瓦的电力供应。",
            "弗吉尼亚州阿什本被认为是全球最大的数据中心集群所在地。"
          ]
        },
        "impact": {
          "en": "These recurring significant power disruptions in a major data center hub highlight critical infrastructure vulnerabilities for the AI industry, which heavily relies on stable and abundant electricity for its operations. The stability of power supply directly influences the reliability and scaling potential of AI computing resources.",
          "zh": "这些在主要数据中心枢纽反复发生的大规模电力中断，凸显了AI行业关键基础设施的脆弱性，该行业严重依赖稳定充沛的电力来支持其运营。电力供应的稳定性直接影响AI计算资源的可靠性和扩展潜力。"
        },
        "source": "MIT Tech Review (AI)",
        "link": "https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/09/10/1141649/powering-ai-is-an-architecture-problem/"
